
The ansi-test are at: "https://gitlab.common-lisp.net/ansi-test/ansi-test"
The ansi-test-harness is at:  "https://github.com/yitzchak/ansi-test-harness.git"

We can use the ansi-test directly quite simply.

    cd ../bocl
    git clone https://gitlab.common-lisp.net/ansi-test/ansi-test
    cd bocl
    sources/bocl --no-init --batch --print -on-error appease -l ../ansi-test/doit.lisp --quit | tee test.out

For now we'll ignore the ansi-test-harness, it's use is when we want
to select some specific tests (and it works with asdf, with the tests
loaded in the lisp image with asdf).



So, I've cloned ansi-test into bocl/../ansi-test ; you can now run them
with bocl using a command such as:

  sources/bocl --no-init --batch --print -on-error appease -l ../ansi-test/doit.lisp --quit

right away we find a warning that seems spurious about -on-error, but
more critical, an error about OR which is not defined
apparently. Anyways, I'll let your run these ansi-test in loop until
you've corrected all the errors (you can leave the conforming problems
alone for now, just ensure that the ansi-test can execute to
completion and print out their report.

